  "body": "Stacked on #3125 (merge #3125 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New function `posting::index_swing::off_origin`. It is true when a rotary states a `pivot` or an `offset` that is not zero, or not finite.\n- The index-swing clause (`posting_index_swing::verdict`) has a new verdict `OffOrigin`. A work-turning rotary with a level line and an off-origin `pivot` or `offset` refuses the post by name. With two or more work-turning rotaries, any off-origin rotary refuses.\n- The posed first-traverse law (`operation::first_traverse_posed::turn_of`) refuses generation by name in the same cases.\n- One vertical work-turning rotary with a pivot is not refused. A turn about a vertical line keeps every height.\n- A zero `pivot` or `offset` is judged as before.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3127-offset-rotary-line.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe two clauses read each work-turning rotary line through the WCS origin. A machine file can state a `pivot` or an `offset` that moves the line. The clauses then read the swept set about the wrong line. The reading can be too low, and the post is not blocked.\n\n`pivot` is in machine coordinates. The project does not state where the WCS origin is in machine coordinates. So the program cannot place the moved line. A refusal is the safe answer.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_posed.rs`:\n  - `a_table_line_off_the_wcs_origin_refuses_by_name` (red before the fix: \"no refusal: Ok []\").\n  - `a_zero_pivot_reads_the_table_line_through_the_wcs_origin` (clear case).\n- `crates/app/tests/index_swing_offset_line.rs` (new file):\n  - `a_pivot_off_the_wcs_origin_refuses_the_index_swing_by_name` (red before the fix).\n  - `an_offset_off_the_wcs_origin_refuses_the_index_swing_by_name` (red before the fix).\n  - `a_zero_pivot_and_offset_judge_the_index_swing_as_before` (clear case; the program posts).\n- Mutation: with the two source files put back to the #3125 head, the three refusal pins fail and the two clear pins pass. With the fix, all five pass.\n- `index_swing` (13) and `first_traverse_posed` (5) pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, local, debug): 9 steps, 0 failed. Steps: app lib, `first_traverse_posed`, `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`, `index_swing_offset_line`, `rotary_subplate`, `rotary_subplate_standing`, `setup_mount_trace`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No shipped machine file states `pivot` or `offset`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The two-rotary branch of `turn_of` with an off-origin rotary has no own pin. It uses the same `off_origin` test as the pinned single-rotary branch.\n- A vertical rotary with a pivot (not refused) has no own pin.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3125: this PR is stacked on it. It changes `turn_of` in `crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs` and adds tests to `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_posed.rs`.\n- #2831 touches `crates/app/tests/index_swing.rs`. This PR puts its index-swing pins in a new file, so there is no overlap.\n\nChangelog: A work-turning rotary whose machine file states a non-zero pivot or offset now refuses the index-swing check and the posed first-traverse check by name, instead of a reading about a line through the WCS origin.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3127\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
